  "fields": [
    {
      "entryId": "ezk-36-26",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "God promises to sprinkle clean water on His people, cleanse them from all idols, take away the stony heart, and give them a heart of flesh, putting His Spirit within them to cause them to walk in His statutes. First principle: regeneration by the Holy Spirit replaces spiritual deadness with responsive obedience.",
      "density": 3.5286,
      "words": 52,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 39,
      "gate": "FAIL",
      "violations": [
        "39 words (max 35): \"God promises to sprinkle clean water on His people, cleanse them from all idols, take away…\""
      ],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "ezk-34-23",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "And I will set up one shepherd over them, and he shall feed them, even my servant David; he shall feed them, and he shall be their shepherd. Spoken against the failed shepherds of Israel who fed themselves. First principle: God answers negligent leadership with a single faithful Shepherd of David's line — and the flock is known by name.",
      "density": 3.1,
      "words": 60,
      "sentences": 3,
      "maxSentenceWords": 28,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "ezk-37-12",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The LORD commands Ezekiel to prophesy to the dry bones in the valley: \"Behold, O My people, I will open your graves, and cause you to come up out of your graves... and put My Spirit in you, and you shall live.\" Jesus echoes this in John 5: all who are in the graves shall hear His voice and come forth. First principle: God's Spirit possesses life-giving power over physical death and national exile.",
      "density": 2.9357,
      "words": 74,
      "sentences": 3,
      "maxSentenceWords": 19,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "ezk-43-2",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Many-waters voice; the earth shined with His glory. First principle: the glory returns by the east gate it left — the same way of departure is the way of return.",
      "density": 2.0071,
      "words": 30,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 22,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "ezk-34-23",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "terms[0].note",
      "text": "The verb ra'ah means both to shepherd and to associate with; Jesus claims the verse in John 10:11-16 and Hebrews 13:20 crowns it.",
      "density": 1.8893,
      "words": 23,
      "sentences": 1,
      "maxSentenceWords": 23,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "term": "feed",
        "original": "וּרְעָם",
        "translit": "ur'am",
        "strongs": null,
        "gloss": "and he shall shepherd them",
        "note": "The verb ra'ah means both to shepherd and to associate with; Jesus claims the verse in John 10:11-16 and Hebrews 13:20 crowns it.",
        "exposition": null
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "ezk-43-7",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Dwelling in the midst forever; the house no more defiled. First principle: throne and soles — sovereignty and nearness in one sentence; the defilement era ends by divine residence.",
      "density": 1.8107,
      "words": 29,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 19,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "ezk-37-27",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The dwelling-promise renewed to resurrected Israel. First principle: tabernacle with them — the covenant formula carried into the valley's aftermath; Revelation quotes it for the redeemed.",
      "density": 1.7929,
      "words": 26,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 20,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "ezk-47-1",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "East-flowing water from the altar side. First principle: the temple leaks life — the trickle at the threshold becomes the knee-deep, hip-deep river of the vision.",
      "density": 1.7929,
      "words": 26,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 20,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "ezk-47-12",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "New fruit by his months; leaf for medicine. First principle: the sanctuary-fed trees never fade — Revelation's tree of life borrows the months and the medicinal leaves.",
      "density": 1.7607,
      "words": 27,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 19,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "ezk-37-5",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Dry bones hear the word and live. First principle: the valley-question answered — breath by word of command; the resurrection preached to an army of bones.",
      "density": 1.7357,
      "words": 26,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 19,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "ezk-34-24",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "God with them, David-prince among them — I the LORD have spoken it. First principle: the divine-shepherd and the David-prince co-reign without contradiction — one flock, both Sheep and Shepherd.",
      "density": 1.7214,
      "words": 30,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 17,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "ezk-36-27",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Statutes kept because the Spirit indwells. First principle: obedience has an internal engine — the cause-you-to-walk is the Spirit's causal presence in the new covenant.",
      "density": 1.7107,
      "words": 25,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 19,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "ezk-40-1",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Twenty-five years after captivity, the hand brings him to the city-smitten land. First principle: the vision-dated tour — the temple-measuring vision answers the glory-departing vision of chapters 10-11.",
      "density": 1.6143,
      "words": 28,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 16,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "ezk-36-25",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Cleansed from filthiness and idols. First principle: the sprinkling is cleansing, not ceremony — idols and filthiness named as what the water washes.",
      "density": 1.6036,
      "words": 23,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 18,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "ezk-37-24",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "One shepherd, judgments walked, statutes done. First principle: the reunited kingdom under the one Shepherd-King — the David-title is the walking-statutes cause.",
      "density": 1.4643,
      "words": 22,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 16,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "ezk-34-11",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The doubled I — God Himself does the seeking the shepherds failed at. First principle: divine intervention replaces negligent leadership — the search is personal, pronoun-emphatic.",
      "density": 1.3929,
      "words": 26,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 13,
      "gate": "PASS",
